A few minutes later, another order arrives.
A customer wants a cappuccino.
I take a deep breath.
I go near the espresso machine.
Now I have to make my second coffee.
I remember my first mistake.
Earlier, the milk had become too hot.
Sunita looks towards me.
She looks at me and smiles.
I am learning to operate this machine.
This time, I do every task carefully.
I make foam in the milk.
I keep full attention on the machine's temperature.
Perfect, the milk is not too hot.
I gently pour the milk over the espresso.
This second coffee turns out very well.
There is perfect foam on top of it.
Sunita says, "Very good, Maya!"
I feel very happy.
I am finally learning to make a good coffee.
